---
// Fig. for "Multivariate & Multilinear Polynomials": moving from one
// variable to several — total degree vs. degree in each variable,
// evaluated at a point (2, 3) in F(13).
---
<svg viewBox="0 0 760 440" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;">
  <text x="380" y="26" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="16" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">from one variable to many</text>

  <rect x="40" y="46" width="680" height="42" rx="10" fill="#111c2e" stroke="#3ab7ff" stroke-width="1.5" />
  <text x="380" y="72" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="13" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">What changes when a polynomial has more than one variable?</text>

  <text x="380" y="122" text-anchor="middle" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">
    <tspan fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700">ONE VARIABLE&#160;&#160;&#160;</tspan><tspan fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700">f(x) = 2 + 3x + x<tspan dy="-6" font-size="65%">2</tspan><tspan dy="6">  (one input, degree 2)</tspan></tspan>
  </text>

  <text x="380" y="154" text-anchor="middle" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">
    <tspan fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700">TWO VARIABLES&#160;&#160;&#160;</tspan><tspan fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700">f(x, y) = 3x<tspan dy="-6" font-size="65%">2</tspan><tspan dy="6">y + 2xy + 5  (the input is a pair (x, y))</tspan></tspan>
  </text>

  <text x="380" y="186" text-anchor="middle" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">
    <tspan fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700">TOTAL DEGREE&#160;&#160;&#160;</tspan><tspan fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700">x<tspan dy="-6" font-size="65%">2</tspan><tspan dy="6">y has degree 2 + 1 = 3, so total degree = 3</tspan></tspan>
  </text>

  <text x="380" y="218" text-anchor="middle" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">
    <tspan fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700">DEGREE IN EACH VARIABLE&#160;&#160;&#160;</tspan><tspan fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700">x &#8594; 2, y &#8594; 1</tspan>
  </text>

  <text x="380" y="250" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11.5" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">EVALUATE AT (2, 3) IN F(13)</text>
  <text x="380" y="276" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">3&#215;2<tspan dy="-6" font-size="65%">2</tspan><tspan dy="6">&#215;3 + 2&#215;2&#215;3 + 5 = 36 + 12 + 5 = 53 = 1</tspan></text>

  <rect x="260" y="298" width="240" height="42" rx="10" fill="#0e1f16" stroke="#5ddc8a" stroke-width="1.8" />
  <text x="380" y="324" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="14.5" font-weight="800" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">f(2, 3) = 1 &#10003;</text>

  <line x1="40" y1="356" x2="720" y2="356" stroke="#223049" stroke-width="1" />
  <text x="380" y="380" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="15.5" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">MANY VARIABLES: ONE POINT IN, ONE NUMBER OUT</text>
  <text x="380" y="402" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12.5" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">Total degree controls how often a random point hits zero.</text>
</svg>
